            <div xml:id="d635">

                <pb facs="0677" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg559"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/314: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-09T14:00:00-05:00">April 9, 1929—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>47. Legation’s eighty-nine, April 8, 9 a.m. The Department assumes that you have
                    conveyed to President Moncada the assurances given by the Brigade Commander as
                    reported in the last paragraph of your telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
